  "behavioral_summary": [
    "Receive time distinguishes modern exact payload (including zero-byte, via PayloadPresent) from legacy payload-less rows; conflicting operation identity, kind, message, payload, or deletion classification fails closed with sentinels.",
    "Exact hash-matching redelivery of a legacy row atomically backfills payload, ForwardDeletionLinks, and pending delete fences; the row stays APPLYING with RecoveredDeletionPending until deletion-only cleanup converges to ApplyStatusFull.",
    "Generic command identity C is NACKed only after convergence; semantic identity D receives its result only from real cleanup. Recovery never fabricates a D-keyed result.",
    "Non-deletion kinds (probe_arm, probe_outcome, node_decommission) regain immediate APPLYING recovery NACK after restart.",
    "Transient convergence failure keeps RecoveredDeletionPending durable across reconnects; the NACKED duplicate branch re-runs convergence before requeueing C.",
    "Post-delete E2E proves listener teardown by exact tcp4 bindability of the published endpoint, and the released tuple is reserved across the restart no-resurrection check so parallel port reuse cannot false-fail or impersonate the deleted Forward.",
    "The local M1 fixture is explicitly non-independent and never claims OPEN_FROM_VANTAGE or public-WAN evidence."
  ],
